 * @subsection FoundationValidationEvidenceArmLocal Arm bare-metal local preflight — 2026-09-25
 *
 * The installed Homebrew `arm-none-eabi-g++` 14.2.0 executable was detected,
 * but its installation has no target C library/sysroot. Compilation therefore
 * stops at the compiler wrapper's `include_next <stdint.h>`. This is recorded
 * as a missing local runtime, not as a Foundation source failure and not as a
 * successful Arm validation. The Ubuntu embedded CI installs
 * `libnewlib-arm-none-eabi` and `libstdc++-arm-none-eabi-newlib` explicitly.
 * Hosted run
 * [36227959989](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36227959989)
 * subsequently built, exported, and inspected all declared Arm profiles. Local
 * firmware linkage and target execution remain separate validation gates.
 *
 * @subsection FoundationValidationEvidenceSTM32G0B1 STM32G0B1CBT6 firmware consumer — 2026-09-28
 *
 * | Field | Recorded value |
 * | ----- | -------------- |
 * | Operator | José Manuel Romo |
 * | Host | macOS Arm64 |
 * | MCU | STM32G0B1CBT6; Cortex-M0+, 128 KiB Flash, up to 144 KiB SRAM |
 * | Preset | `stm32g0b1cbt6_armgcc_cortex_m0plus_soft` |
 * | Toolchain | Arm GNU Toolchain 15.3.Rel1 with Newlib, extracted locally without a system-wide installation |
 * | Package | Fresh Release export; identity validator confirmed ELF32 little-endian Armv6S-M, soft-float, 4-byte pointers, and no Debug import |
 * | Consumer | `tests/Stm32G0B1Consumer`, found through `find_package(Foundation 1.2 CONFIG REQUIRED)` and linked only through `Foundation::Foundation` |
 * | Firmware | 2696-byte ELF image; 2668 bytes text, 16 bytes initialized data, 12 bytes BSS; HEX, BIN, and linker map generated |
 * | Memory contract | 64-byte vector table at `0x08000000`; code in 128 KiB Flash; data begins at `0x20000000`; first 128 KiB SRAM used conservatively |
 * | ABI and link inspection | ELF32/Arm executable, Armv6S-M, Thumb-1, soft-float, no undefined symbols; map pulls `Frequency.cpp` and `Period.cpp` from the exported `libFoundation.a` |
 * | Runtime contract | Fourteen representative Math, Time, Containers, Functional, and Utils checks update `FoundationValidationPassed`, `FoundationValidationTotal`, and `FoundationValidationState`; completion executes `bkpt` for SWD inspection |
 * | Hosted reproduction | [Run 36445860085](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36445860085) rebuilt all nine Arm packages and passed the STM32G0B1 package, link, ELF, map, and artifact checks on commit `f8b1f50` |
 * | Not yet proven | Flashing and execution on the physical STM32G0B1CBT6; this is required before VAL-008 can be `DONE` |
 *
 * @subsection FoundationValidationEvidencePackageIdentity Package identity — 2026-09-26
 *
 * The repository-owned identity gate passed on all seven hosted native package
 * identities in
 * [run 36267812890](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36267812890)
 * and on AVR plus all eight declared Arm profiles in
 * [run 36267813048](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36267813048).
 * The native matrix also proved that the validator rejects an added Debug
 * archive, a missing public header, and altered build-identity metadata. This
 * closes package structure and binary identity; firmware linkage, emulator, and
 * hardware execution remain separate evidence.
 *
 * @subsection FoundationValidationEvidenceNativeExamples Hosted native examples — 2026-09-27
 *
 * Main-branch
 * [run 36375583593](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36375583593)
 * validated commit `8c2ec36` with the repository-owned example validators.
 * The validators discover the 12 desktop example definitions instead of using
 * a hardcoded executable list.
 *
 * | Field | Recorded value |
 * | ----- | -------------- |
 * | Windows MSVC x64 | All 12 examples built and exited 0 in Debug and Release; stdout and stderr matched; the Release-only export passed identity validation; all 12 exported executables ran with matching output; scripted quit and first-example scenarios passed through `FoundationExamples.cmd` |
 * | Windows Clang x64 | Passed the same build, execution, output, export, and `.cmd` launcher checks |
 * | Linux GCC x64 | All 12 examples built and exited 0 in Debug and Release; output matched; the Release-only export passed identity validation; all 12 exported executables ran with matching output; the export correctly contained no desktop launcher |
 * | Linux Clang x64 | Passed the same build, execution, output, export, and no-launcher checks |
 * | Additional coverage | macOS Arm64 plus Linux GCC/Clang Arm64 passed the same applicable automated workflow in the run |
 * | Not covered | Opening `FoundationExamples.cmd` manually through Windows Explorer; unsigned-download security prompts |
 *
 * This closes VAL-005. VAL-003 and VAL-004 retain only the manual Explorer
 * user-experience check; their compiler, test, package, example, and scripted
 * launcher gates pass on the GitHub-hosted Windows runner.
 *
 * @subsection FoundationValidationEvidenceReleasedConsumer Published v1.2.0 downstream consumer — 2026-09-27
 *
 * The public macOS Arm64 release asset was downloaded from
 * [Foundation v1.2.0](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/releases/tag/v1.2.0)
 * into a new directory under `/private/tmp`, outside the Foundation checkout.
 * Its published checksum file verified SHA-256
 * `69fa1d44db8186b5bf55a4571a0f7f4cd51ef0e0fd0c86d04066f16aea33b1b7`.
 *
 * A new external CMake project, also outside the checkout, requested
 * `Foundation 1.2.0 EXACT` and received the package only through
 * `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` pointing at the extracted archive. It included
 * `Foundation.h` plus selective Time headers, used the v1.2.0 `FloorDiv` and
 * `FloorMod` APIs in constant expressions, and linked
 * `Foundation::Foundation`. The resulting Arm64 executable contained the
 * out-of-line `Frequency::GetPeriod()` and `Period::GetFrequency()` symbols and
 * passed its registered test 1/1.
 *
 * The consumer source, CMake cache, compile commands, and Ninja graph contained
 * no path to the Foundation checkout. No source, build tree, package metadata,
 * or other unreleased file from `main` participated in configuration,
 * compilation, linking, or execution. This closes REL-005 for the published
 * release; the release matrix already validates the equivalent package shape
 * on the other published native platforms before publication.
 */
